BasisDefinition opnormbound, normbound
Failing due to a delicate issue, while L1 is a subtype of NormKind,  Type{L1} is not a subtype of Type{NormKind}

AnnulusGeometry.jl, EllipseGeometry.jl: enclose T on the boundary path by Taylor models
The boundary checks evaluate T directly on boxes covering the arcs.  TaylorModels 0.10 has
elementary functions (exp, sin, cos, ...) on real models only: on a complex model exp fails
(no _rpa method for Complex{Interval}).  Route: carry Re T and Im T on the line Im x = b as
two real TaylorModel1 in x, which needs T given by its two parts.  Further: TaylorModels
with BallArithmetic coefficients, and complex rpa.
